<h3>LED Status</h3>

<p>This plugin shows the OctoPrint/printer state on the appliance LEDs.</p>

<table class="table table-condensed">
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>State</th>
      <th>Red</th>
      <th>Green</th>
      <th>Blue</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td>Startup / disconnected / error</td>
      <td>On</td>
      <td>Off</td>
      <td>Fast blink</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Idle / ready</td>
      <td>On</td>
      <td>On</td>
      <td>Off</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Printing</td>
      <td>On</td>
      <td>On</td>
      <td>On</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Paused</td>
      <td>On</td>
      <td>On</td>
      <td>Slow blink</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Shutdown</td>
      <td>Off</td>
      <td>Off</td>
      <td>Off</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<p class="muted">
  Uses <code>/usr/local/sbin/led-helper</code> via sudo. No settings here; this page is informational.
</p>
